All 15 tests pass. Here's what was wrong and what I changed:

**`src/auth.py`** (`has_permission`, `is_admin_or_owner`)
- Role comparison was case-sensitive; fixed by lowercasing both sides (`any(role.lower() == required.lower() …)`).
- `is_admin_or_owner` used `and` instead of `or`, so you had to be both admin AND owner. Changed to `or`.

**`src/inventory.py`** (`Inventory.__init__`, `add`, `reserve`, `release`)
- Mutable default argument `={}` caused instances to share stock. Replaced with `None` + `dict(initial) if initial else {}`.
- `add` overwrote quantity instead of accumulating. Changed to `self._stock[sku] = self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty`.
- `reserve` raised `OutOfStock` when `qty >= available`; changed to `>` so reserving exactly the available amount is allowed.
- `release` didn't guard against releasing more than was reserved. Added a check that raises `ValueError` if `qty > current`.

**`src/text_utils.py`** (`slugify`, `truncate`)
- `slugify` didn't lowercase letters. Now appends `char.lower()` for alnum characters.
- Non-alphanumeric characters (including `!`, `,`) now become `-` instead of being silently skipped, and all consecutive dashes are collapsed with a `while "--" in …` loop.
- `truncate` sliced `text[:max_len]` and then appended the suffix, exceeding `max_len`. Fixed to `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix` so the total length respects the limit.
